---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';

const TILES = [
  { id: 'advances', label: 'Advancing', note: 'Closed above the session before', spark: true },
  { id: 'declines', label: 'Declining', note: 'Closed below the session before', spark: true },
  { id: 'ratio', label: 'A / D ratio', note: 'Risers per faller · 1.00 is even', spark: true },
  { id: 'lifter', label: 'Biggest lifter', note: '—' },
  { id: 'dragger', label: 'Biggest dragger', note: '—' },
  { id: 'estimate', label: 'Our estimate', note: '—' },
];
---
<Base title="Market Map" current="map"
  description="One trading session of the Jakarta Composite Index (IHSG) at a time: which stocks moved it, a map of every index stock, the top lists and sector rotation.">

  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="kicker">Market Map · one session at a time</div>
      <h1>What moved the Jakarta market</h1>
      <p class="dek">Pick any session of the last year — with the date control below, or by clicking a candle — and read
        which stocks moved the IHSG, how every index stock fared, and where each sector stands against the whole.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="hero" aria-label="The session on show">
      <div class="hero-lead">
        <div class="hero-label">IHSG close · <span id="hero-date">latest session</span></div>
        <div class="hero-figure index" id="hero-close">—</div>
        <div class="hero-verdict" id="hero-move">Awaiting the session</div>
        <dl class="hero-meta">
          <div><dt>Day's range</dt><dd id="hero-range">—</dd></div>
          <div><dt>% Advancing</dt><dd><a href="/breadth.html" id="hero-pctadv">—</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="tiles">
        {TILES.map(t => (
          <div class="tile">
            <div class="tile-label">{t.label}</div>
            <div class="tile-value" id={t.id}>—</div>
            {t.spark && <svg class="tile-spark" id={`${t.id}-spark`} aria-hidden="true"></svg>}
            <div class="tile-note" id={t.spark ? undefined : `${t.id}-note`}>{t.note}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="toolbar">
    <div class="wrap">
      <!-- The session on show: drives the headline, the tiles, Who moved it,
           the session map and the rotation. Click any candle to pick one too. -->
      <div class="session-nav" role="group" aria-label="Session on show">
        <span class="toolbar-label" id="session-label">Session</span>
        <button type="button" class="movers-btn" id="session-prev" aria-label="Previous session">‹</button>
        <input type="date" class="movers-input" id="session-day" aria-labelledby="session-label">
        <button type="button" class="movers-btn" id="session-next" aria-label="Next session">›</button>
        <button type="button" class="link-btn" id="session-latest" hidden>Latest</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <Figure no="Fig. I" title="The index itself" chart="ihsg" size="tall"
      dek="The IHSG, one candle per session. It weighs each company by its freely traded value, so a few of the largest move it — beneath, the ones that did.">
      <div class="movers" id="movers" hidden>
        <div class="movers-head">
          <h3>Who moved it</h3>
          <div class="tabs" role="group" aria-label="Rank the session by">
            <button type="button" data-view="points" aria-pressed="true">Index points</button>
            <button type="button" data-view="price" aria-pressed="false">Price %</button>
            <button type="button" data-view="activity" aria-pressed="false">Value &amp; volume</button>
          </div>
          <div class="tabs" role="group" aria-label="Read one session or a date range">
            <button type="button" id="movers-mode-day" aria-pressed="true">One day</button>
            <button type="button" id="movers-mode-range" aria-pressed="false">Date range</button>
          </div>
          <span class="movers-pick" id="movers-pick-range" hidden>
            <input type="date" class="movers-input" id="movers-from" aria-label="From date">
            <span class="movers-to">to</span>
            <input type="date" class="movers-input" id="movers-to" aria-label="To date">
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="movers-title">
          <span class="movers-date" id="movers-date">—</span>
          <span class="movers-move" id="movers-move"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="movers-cols">
          <div class="movers-col up">
            <div class="movers-col-head" id="movers-head-up">Lifted the index · points</div>
            <ol class="movers-list" id="movers-up"></ol>
          </div>
          <div class="movers-col down">
            <div class="movers-col-head" id="movers-head-down">Dragged it · points</div>
            <ol class="movers-list" id="movers-down"></ol>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="link-btn" id="movers-more" hidden>Show 20</button>
        <p class="movers-foot" id="movers-foot"></p>
        <details class="how">
          <summary>How the attribution is estimated</summary>
          <p>Each stock's points are its weight going into the session times its own move. The weights are rebuilt
            from Yahoo share counts and public free-float figures refreshed monthly (latest
            <span id="movers-float-asof">—</span>), not IDX's own, so they can miss the real move by a few points — the
            gap is printed above. Stocks IDX flags for concentrated ownership no longer count toward the index from
            their effective date. A date range adds up each stock's points over its sessions, and shows its own price
            move across them. Covers the last year of sessions. Hover any candle to read that session.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <Fragment slot="how">
        <p>The body of each candle spans open to close, the wick the day's full range. Green closed up, red closed
          down. The <a href="/breadth.html">Breadth &amp; Momentum</a> page checks the index against everyone else.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>

    <Figure no="Fig. II" title="The session map"
      dek="Every index stock, sized by its weight in the IHSG and coloured by its own move, grouped by sector. Hover or tap a block.">
      <Fragment slot="legend">
        <span class="legend-key"><span class="sw" style="background:#b0392c"></span>−5%</span>
        <span class="legend-key"><span class="sw" style="background:#ded6c7"></span>0</span>
        <span class="legend-key"><span class="sw" style="background:#2f6b4f"></span>+5%</span>
      </Fragment>
      <div class="readout-line">
        <span class="kicker" id="hm-label">—</span>
        <span id="hm-readout">Loading the session…</span>
      </div>
      <svg id="heatmap" class="heatmap" role="img" aria-labelledby="hm-alt" preserveAspectRatio="none"></svg>
      <p id="hm-alt" class="visually-hidden"></p>
      <Fragment slot="how">
        <p>A block's area is the stock's free-float weight in our rebuild of the IHSG going into the session — the same
          weights as Who moved it — so the big blocks are the ones that can move the index. Colour runs from red at −5% to
          green at +5% and beyond. Sectors are Yahoo Finance's; a stock it doesn't classify sits under Other.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>

    <Figure no="Fig. III" title="Sector rotation"
      dek="Each sector's strength against the index (across) and whether it is gaining or losing that strength (up), week by week. The dot is the latest week, the tail the five before.">
      <div class="readout-line">
        <span class="kicker" id="rot-label">Sectors</span>
        <span id="rot-readout">Hover a sector.</span>
      </div>
      <svg id="rotation" class="rotation" role="img" aria-labelledby="rot-alt" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"></svg>
      <p id="rot-alt" class="visually-hidden"></p>
      <ul class="rot-legend" id="rot-legend"></ul>
      <Fragment slot="how">
        <p>Sectors usually turn clockwise: Improving → Leading → Weakening → Lagging. The axes approximate J. de
          Kempenaer's Relative Rotation Graph, whose exact formula is proprietary: relative strength is each sector's
          index against the whole, divided by its own 10-week average; momentum is that figure's change on the week.
          Sector indices are rebuilt from the same free-float weights as Who moved it, so read the positions as
          relative, not as IDX's official sector indices.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>
  </div>

  <script src="../lib/market.js"></script>
</Base>
